{"name":"Liqueur Red","hex":"#61394b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"liqueur","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flavored alcoholic beverage that is usually very sweet and contains a high percentage of alcohol."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["to flavor or treat (wine) with a liqueur","to top up bottles of sparkling wine with a sugar solution"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/liqueur"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Liqueur","blocks":[{"text":"A liqueur or cordial is an alcoholic drink composed of spirits and additional flavorings such as sugar, fruits, herbs, and spices. Often served with or after dessert, they are typically heavily sweetened and un-aged, beyond a resting period during production, when necessary, for their flavors to mingle."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/92/Licor-Beir%C3%A3o-%26-Orus_-_Orus_Clothing_%28cropped%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liqueur","wikidata":"Q178780"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Benedictine_01_08.jpg/500px-Benedictine_01_08.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Benedictine_01_08.jpg/500px-Benedictine_01_08.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bénédictine, a traditional French herbal liqueur","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABenedictine_01_08.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3a/Cocktail_B52.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3a/Cocktail_B52.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"The B-52 is a layered drink prepared using Grand Marnier atop Irish cream over a base of coffee liqueur","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACocktail_B52.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Altvater_Gessler.JPG/120px-Altvater_Gessler.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Altvater_Gessler.JPG/250px-Altvater_Gessler.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Altvater_Gessler.JPG/120px-Altvater_Gessler.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en